  "query": "What output does the standby magnetic compass provide?",
  "final_answer": "FINAL ANSWER  \nThe standby magnetic compass provides magnetic heading (direction relative to magnetic north) via the needle aligning with the local magnetic field.  \n\n- It displays the aircraft's magnetic heading using a rotating needle on a dial marked with degrees and cardinal directions [page:1, stable_id:10ad72b0f4bf71b9].  \n- The dial includes degree markings (e.g., 30\u00b0 increments) and a cardinal indicator (N) for reference [page:1, stable_id:dbf3ecf3a5add564].",
